      "description": "Turn your iPhone, iPad or Mac into a live companion display for Microsoft Flight Simulator with live telemetry, maps, customizable gauges, airport information, weather, flight statistics, approach helpers, missions and challenges—all without leaving the simulator window.\n\nSee your aircraft position on the map, monitor altitude, heading, airspeed, ground speed and vertical speed, browse airports, inspect runways, check live airport weather and use visual approach helpers while you fly.\n\nTake on Missions & Challenges and give your flights a destination. Choose from included challenges or download additional mission packs, explore airports around the world and complete each objective by flying there in Microsoft Flight Simulator. Avionics Buddy automatically recognizes your landings, tracks your challenge progress and awards medals as you complete them.\n\nAvionics Buddy is built for sim pilots who want to extend their Microsoft Flight Simulator setup beyond the main screen. Use it as a beautifully designed cockpit display on your desk or as an additional avionics screen in a larger multi-monitor simulator setup. Its adaptive interface makes use of the available screen space across iPhone, iPad and Mac, letting you build your own flight deck using the Apple devices you already own.\n\nTrack your current flight with the Trip Computer, including distance, fuel, speed, altitude, wind and temperature. Continue building your Lifetime Logbook with accumulated flight time, takeoffs, landings, distance flown and personal records across all your simulator sessions.\n\nSearch more than 80,000 airports, save your favorites, display selected airports on the map, inspect runways and review live weather before departure. Export and import your Airport Library to back up your saved airports or transfer them between your iPhone, iPad and Mac.\n\nStay connected to your flight, even when Microsoft Flight Simulator is running on another screen.\n\nKey Features\n\n• Missions & Challenges with automatic landing detection, progress tracking and medals\n• Downloadable mission packs with detailed mission briefings – https://www.avionicsbuddy.com/missions/\n• Live aircraft telemetry from Microsoft Flight Simulator\n• Follow-mode map with aircraft position, heading and selectable aircraft icons\n• Customizable cockpit gauges with multiple layouts, styles and live Session Gauge metrics\n• Trip Computer with live flight statistics for every session\n• Lifetime Logbook with cumulative flight time, takeoffs, landings, distance and records\n• Awards and medals earned through your flying\n• Search over 80,000 airports with favorites and map integration\n• Export and import your Airport Library between Apple devices\n• Runway approach helpers for visual alignment during simulator arrivals\n• Live airport weather with wind, pressure, clouds and current conditions\n• Optional cabin sound effects, including seatbelt announcements and other immersive details\n• Adaptive layouts across iPhone, iPad and Apple Silicon Mac\n• Local network connection through the free Avionics Buddy Bridge for Windows\n• No account required\n• No cloud telemetry\n\nHow it works\n\n1. Start Microsoft Flight Simulator on your Windows PC.\n2. Download and run the free Avionics Buddy Bridge for Windows – https://www.avionicsbuddy.com/#bridge\n3. Scan the QR code with Avionics Buddy on your iPhone, iPad or Mac.\n4. Fly with live telemetry on your second screen.\n\nAvionics Buddy is intended for Microsoft Flight Simulator entertainment use only. It is not designed for real-world navigation, flight training, flight planning or operational aviation use. Avionics Buddy is not affiliated with Microsoft, Asobo Studio, Working Title, OurAirports or any aircraft manufacturer.",
